  "body": "Uncommitted hgraph churn is back: 1,426 modified node files, ~8,900 untracked, and 4 nodes lost real prose\n\nThe workspace ledger worktree carries a large uncommitted `hgraph` diff. `I-0311` (destructive slice sync) was archived 2026-07-24 as \"already handled in current code\"; the *symptom* has recurred, so either the fix is incomplete or something else is rewriting the graph. Filed for a graph owner, not fixed here — the janitor did not sync, stage, revert, or commit any graph path.\n\n**Snapshot (2026-07-25 21:00, runs `0046` and `0047` both live):**\n\n- `MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/hgraph` — **1,362** modified tracked nodes\n- `MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph` — **64** modified tracked nodes\n- Six subproject `hgraph/` trees are **entirely untracked** (~8,900 files): Cech-Cohomology 2,581, GR-Quot-Closure 2,460, Line-Bundle-Comparison-Iso 1,747, MR0555258 924, Albanese 753, Picard-IdentityComponent 435\n\n**Almost all of it is noise.** Of 2,804 insertions / 2,884 deletions, **2,876 changed lines are the `updated:` timestamp** and **2,642 are `order:`, every one an off-by-one bump** (`1033`→`1034`, `714`→`715`, `1629`→`1630`, …) — a global renumber from one node inserted near the front, not real content. Only **17 files** have more than 2 changed lines.\n\n**Four of those 17 are net content loss**, and it is not timestamp noise. `hgraph/nodes/a779f7b7a74d.md` (`rmk:rigidity_lemma_decomposition`) drops **43 lines for 6**: the entire iter-161 status record — bridge-1 `snd_left_isClosedMap` closed, bridge-2 split into the proved globalisation `lem:morphism_eq_of_eqAt_closedPoints` and the single deep residual `lem:rigidity_eqAt_closedPoint_of_proper_into_affine`, and the reasoning for carrying **both** `[IsAlgClosed k̄]` and `[LocallyOfFiniteType]` across the chain. Its `chapter:` field is also truncated (\"…and its Milne \\S I.1--I.3 corollaries\" → \"…and its corollaries\"). Same shape in `3b980b9257c0.md` (4/13), `33cb4a20bee8.md` (2/12), `d583446886fc.md` (2/10).\n\n**Next action for a graph owner:** decide whether the four content-losing nodes are an intended prose canonicalization or collateral from a regeneration, and recover the rigidity decomposition note if the latter. Then either commit the graph state as a reviewed graph-only commit or discard it; leaving ~1,400 modified files in the shared worktree means every session commits against ambiguous graph state, and `I-0157`-style accidental staging becomes likely. Note `I-0318` (the rebuild has no `hgraph/config.yaml`) is probably the same job.",
